motions.source_motion_text:
THAT Council adopt "Amenity Cost Charge Bylaw No. 2275, 2026";
             AND
             THAT Council adopt "Inclusionary Zoning Bylaw No. 2270, 2026";
             AND
             THAT Council adopt “City of Langford Reserve Funds Establishment Bylaw, 2004, Bylaw
             No. 857, Amendment No. 3, Bylaw No. 2271, 2026”.

THAT Council close the meeting to the public pursuant to section 90 (1) (e), (g) and (i) of the
       Community Charter to consider:

           •   the acquisition, disposition or expropriation of land or improvements;

           •   litigation or potential litigation affecting the municipality;

           •   the receipt of advice that is subject to solicitor-client privilege, including
               communications necessary for that purpose.

THAT Council consider giving first reading to Bylaw 2031 as drafted;

           AND

           THAT Council direct staff to host an information session with members of the
           development community and public to establish DP Area Climate Action parameters
           prior to bringing forward draft DP guidelines for Council's review;

THAT Council adopt "Animal Control Miscellaneous Amending Bylaw No. 2212, 2026";

             AND

             THAT Council adopt "Animal Responsibility Bylaw No. 2239, 2026".

THAT Council adopt “City of Langford 2026-2030 Financial Plan Bylaw No. 2281, 2026”;
               AND
               "City of Langford Tax Rates Bylaw No. 2282, 2026".

THAT Council adopt “Community Standards Bylaw No. 2255, 2026”;
       AND
       “Community Standards Miscellaneous Amending Bylaw, No. 2262, 2026”.
